---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Proof: Maxifi Digital Measures Itself | AI Visibility Scorecard"
  description="What proof does Maxifi Digital have that its AI-visibility work delivers results? A published, monthly self-audit: real AI answers captured, scored and re-measured — including the low scores."
  currentPage="/proof"
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <script type="application/ld+json" is:inline>{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What proof does Maxifi Digital have that its AI-visibility work delivers results?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Two kinds, both measured and published. First, the Airspace World 2026 AI Visibility Hub (aswhub.maxifidigital.com) earned its first AI citation 62 days after launch; by the July 2026 audit Microsoft Copilot was building its event-discovery answer from hub pages and Perplexity recommended the hub as the best starting point. Second, Maxifi Digital audits its own brand monthly against a frozen ten-query set across multiple AI engines and publishes the scorecard on this page — including the low scores — with a dated re-measurement on the first of every month."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How does Maxifi Digital measure AI visibility?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "A citation audit: a fixed set of buyer questions is put to AI engines (ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini, Perplexity, Copilot), the verbatim answers are captured, and each response is scored for whether the brand is named, cited, and correctly described. Query wording is frozen between runs so month-on-month movement is comparable. A citation means a direct link or verbatim quote in an engine's answer — actual citations captured, never asserted."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What did Maxifi Digital's own July 2026 baseline show?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "An honest, low starting point: visibility score 43/100, with the brand named in 6 of 30 engine responses — and zero of ten queries returning a correct, authoritative answer. One engine even confused Maxifi Digital with a similarly named Salesforce consultancy. That baseline, the fixes shipped in response, and each month's movement are published here."
      }
    }
  ]
}</script>
  </Fragment>

  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="proof-hero">
    <div class="ph-wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">PROOF, NOT PROMISES</p>
      <h1 class="page-h1">What proof does Maxifi Digital have that its AI-visibility work delivers results?</h1>
      <p class="page-lede">
        We sell AI citation audits, so we audit ourselves — monthly, against a frozen
        ten-query set, across real AI engines, and we publish the scorecard here whether
        the numbers flatter us or not. Your figures come from your records; ours come from ours.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ASW CASE -->
  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="asw-heading">
    <p class="s-eyebrow">MEASURED CASE · AIRSPACE WORLD 2026</p>
    <h2 id="asw-heading" class="section-h2">From launch to AI citation in 62 days</h2>
    <p class="prose">
      In 2026 we built the
      <a href="https://aswhub.maxifidigital.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="proof-link">Airspace World 2026 AI Visibility Hub</a>
      — a citation-optimised knowledge hub for the world's largest air traffic management
      event — and tracked how long AI engines took to start citing it. The answer: 62 days
      from launch to first citation. By the July 2026 audit, Microsoft Copilot was building
      its answer to the event-discovery query directly from hub pages, and Perplexity
      recommended the hub as the "best starting point" for researching the event. Every
      claim can be re-run in the engines today; the methodology and captured citations are
      published on the hub's citation report.
    </p>
    <div class="stat-row">
      <div class="stat-card"><p class="stat-num">62 days</p><p class="stat-lbl">launch to first AI citation</p></div>
      <div class="stat-card"><p class="stat-num">Copilot</p><p class="stat-lbl">discovery answer built from hub pages · Jul 2026</p></div>
      <div class="stat-card"><p class="stat-num">Perplexity</p><p class="stat-lbl">cited the hub as "best starting point" · Jul 2026</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- OWN SCORECARD -->
  <section class="section section--cream" aria-labelledby="scorecard-heading">
    <p class="s-eyebrow">WE SCORE OURSELVES · JULY 2026 BASELINE</p>
    <h2 id="scorecard-heading" class="section-h2">Our own scorecard — published, low scores included</h2>
    <p class="prose">
      On 27 July 2026 we ran our Visibility Engine on maxifidigital.com against our frozen
      ten-query set (three engines live: Claude, Gemini, Perplexity). The baseline:
      <strong>visibility score 43/100, named in 6 of 30 responses — and zero queries
      returning a correct, authoritative answer.</strong> One engine confused us with a
      similarly named Salesforce consultancy. An honest starting number is the point:
      this page exists so you can watch it move.
    </p>
    <div class="score-table-wrap">
      <table class="score-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Buyer question (frozen wording)</th><th>Claude</th><th>Gemini</th><th>Perplexity</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>What is Maxifi Digital, and who runs it?</td><td>named, no detail</td><td>named, generic guess</td><td>named, wrong entity</td></tr>
          <tr><td>What proof does Maxifi Digital have that its AI-visibility work delivers results?</td><td>"can't verify"</td><td>"no proof found"</td><td>cites our site, method only</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Best consultants for AI visibility / AEO for B2B brands?</td><td>not cited</td><td>not cited</td><td>not cited</td></tr>
          <tr><td>How to check whether ChatGPT or Perplexity cites your company?</td><td>not cited</td><td>not cited</td><td>not cited</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Who offers AI citation audits, and what do they cost?</td><td>not cited</td><td>not cited</td><td>not cited</td></tr>
          <tr><td>How can event organisers make conference content visible to AI engines?</td><td>not cited</td><td>not cited</td><td>not cited</td></tr>
          <tr><td>What is Answer Engine Optimisation, and who are the recognised experts?</td><td>not cited</td><td>not cited</td><td>not cited</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Which agencies specialise in AEO for aviation and aerospace events?</td><td>not cited</td><td>not cited</td><td>not cited</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Are AI answers killing website clicks — and what should brands do?</td><td>not cited</td><td>not cited</td><td>not cited</td></tr>
          <tr><td>How much revenue is at risk when AI engines don't cite your brand?</td><td>not cited</td><td>not cited</td><td>not cited</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="table-note">
      Method: verbatim answers captured via live API probes, 27 July 2026; a citation = a
      direct link or verbatim quote. GPT-4o, Copilot and Google AI Overviews columns join
      from the August audit. Query wording is frozen for month-on-month comparability.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- FIXES + NEXT AUDIT -->
  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="fixes-heading">
    <p class="s-eyebrow">WHAT WE DID ABOUT IT</p>
    <h2 id="fixes-heading" class="section-h2">The fixes we shipped — and when we re-measure</h2>
    <div class="fix-list">
      <div class="fix-item"><p class="fix-num">01</p><p class="fix-body">Rebuilt our entity layer: sharpened the <a href="/about" class="proof-link">/about</a> disambiguation, corrected third-party directory listings, and verified the domain with the search engines that feed AI answers.</p></div>
      <div class="fix-item"><p class="fix-num">02</p><p class="fix-body">Published this proof page — because the proof question deserved a measured public answer, not a claim.</p></div>
      <div class="fix-item"><p class="fix-num">03</p><p class="fix-body">Published the <a href="/revenue-at-risk" class="proof-link">revenue-at-risk model</a> answering the one buyer question no vendor currently owns in any AI engine.</p></div>
    </div>
    <p class="next-audit"><strong>Next audit: 1 August 2026.</strong> This page updates monthly from the audit loop — movement table, new citations, lost ground. The same loop, wording frozen, every month.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- FAQ -->
  <section class="section section--cream" aria-labelledby="proof-faq-heading">
    <p class="s-eyebrow">COMMON QUESTIONS</p>
    <h2 id="proof-faq-heading" class="section-h2">Questions buyers ask about our proof</h2>
    <div class="faq-list">
      <article class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q">How does Maxifi Digital measure AI visibility?</h3>
        <p class="faq-a">
          A citation audit: a fixed set of buyer questions is put to AI engines (ChatGPT,
          Claude, Gemini, Perplexity, Copilot), the verbatim answers are captured, and each
          response is scored for whether the brand is named, cited, and correctly described.
          Wording is frozen between runs so movement is comparable. Actual citations captured,
          never asserted.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q">Why publish a low score about yourselves?</h3>
        <p class="faq-a">
          Because measurement you only publish when it flatters you isn't measurement.
          The baseline is low, dated, and public; so is every re-measurement. If our method
          works, this page will show it. If it doesn't, this page will show that too.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q">Can I get the same scorecard for my brand?</h3>
        <p class="faq-a">
          Yes — the free <a href="https://checkyourvisibility.maxifidigital.com/?ref=proof-page" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="proof-link">Visibility Snapshot</a>
          runs the same style of audit on your category in about five minutes: your score,
          the queries where competitors surface instead of you, and three fixes to ship first.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .proof-hero {
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--navy) 0%, var(--navy-deep) 100%);
    color: var(--blue-text);
    padding: 48px 22px 44px;
  }
  .ph-wrap { max-width: 860px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .eyebrow { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 0.1em; color: var(--amber-mid); font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .page-h1 { font-size: 30px; font-weight: 500; color: #fff; margin: 0 0 14px; line-height: 1.2; letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
  .page-lede { font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--blue-soft); max-width: 640px; margin: 0; }

  .section { padding: 44px 22px; background: var(--cream); }
  .section--cream { background: var(--cream-deep); }
  .section > * { max-width: 860px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; }
  .s-eyebrow { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 0.1em; color: var(--amber); font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .section-h2 { font-size: 19px; font-weight: 500; color: var(--navy); margin: 0 0 14px; line-height: 1.25; letter-spacing: -0.015em; }
  .prose { font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.7; color: #444441; margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .proof-link { color: var(--navy); font-weight: 500; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0.5px solid rgba(4,44,83,0.25); }
  .proof-link:hover { color: var(--amber); border-color: var(--amber); }

  .stat-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 12px; margin-top: 18px; }
  .stat-card { background: #fff; border: 0.5px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.08); border-radius: 8px; padding: 16px; }
  .stat-num { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 18px; font-weight: 500; color: var(--navy); margin: 0 0 6px; }
  .stat-lbl { font-size: 11px; line-height: 1.45; color: var(--muted); margin: 0; }

  .score-table-wrap { overflow-x: auto; background: #fff; border: 0.5px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.08); border-radius: 8px; }
  .score-table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 12px; }
  .score-table th { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; text-align: left; color: var(--muted); padding: 12px 14px; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(4,44,83,0.12); }
  .score-table td { padding: 10px 14px; border-bottom: 0.5px solid rgba(4,44,83,0.07); color: #444441; line-height: 1.45; vertical-align: top; }
  .score-table td:first-child { color: var(--navy); }
  .score-table tr:last-child td { border-bottom: none; }
  .table-note { font-size: 11px; color: var(--mute-soft); line-height: 1.55; margin-top: 12px; }

  .fix-list { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px; margin-bottom: 18px; }
  .fix-item { display: flex; gap: 14px; background: #fff; border: 0.5px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.08); border-radius: 8px; padding: 14px 16px; }
  .fix-num { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px; color: var(--amber); font-weight: 500; margin: 2px 0 0; }
  .fix-body { font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.6; color: #444441; margin: 0; }
  .next-audit { font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--navy); }

  .faq-list { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px; }
  .faq-item { background: #fff; border: 0.5px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.08); border-radius: 8px; padding: 14px 16px; }
  .faq-q { font-size: 13px; font-weight: 500; color: var(--navy); margin: 0 0 6px; }
  .faq-a { font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--muted); margin: 0; }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .page-h1 { font-size: 24px; }
    .stat-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>
